WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:05.400
Across Cameroon the level of unemployment
is around 30 percent.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.540
Some analysts believe the real figure is much higher.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:17.260
Many people have to take on informal jobs
like motor taxi driving to make ends meet.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:22.480
Even highly skilled workers like Sakwe Njayo
have problems finding a real job.

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:34.980
“You are just from High school or any professional
school and did internship for like three months

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:37.660
but you are still looking for a job.”

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.140
The job market in Cameroon is complicated.

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:45.500
Workers and entrepreneurs can't establish contact easily.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:51.040
That's why start-up founder Churchill Mambe
Nanje had to find a solution.

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:54.840
“It was very difficult for me to find new
developers.

00:00:54.850 --> 00:01:00.170
So I thought it wise that if I build a platform
where there would be a database of profiles

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:03.960
that I could search through, that's what led
me to njorku.com.“

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:09.260
In 2012 he created a job page named
njorku.com -

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:13.460
with massive success. It is now among Africa’s
biggest job search engines.

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:16.360
“Njorku is an aggregator just like Google.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:23.270
So we go to other job sites and other websites
and find jobs and career pages of companies

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:32.500
then aggregate job content and bring it in
one location.”

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:38.220
Churchill collects job adverts from other
job sites and puts them on Njorku.

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:43.130
Two hundred thousand people search for jobs
each month and over 2 million job records

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:44.960
can be found on Njorku.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:49.670
Software engineers like Sakwe Njayo use the
website to upload their resumees.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:58.659
“When I tell someone that I studied in India
they raise their eyebrows in surprise, and

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:02.280
the next question that comes out is how much?”

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:07.380
Skilled workers expect higher wages and this
is another reason why unemployment remains

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:09.929
high and is a big challenge for families in Cameroon.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:15.099
“When they are not working after spending
so much money on them, they come back home

00:02:15.099 --> 00:02:20.180
and sit in the house and you keep feeding
and clothing them and even providing them

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:23.920
with to money to go and search the internet
for jobs.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:25.200
So it’s really a burden to all the parents.”

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:31.100
But Njorku.com still is a success and brings
together employees and businessmen.

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:34.890
Even if Churchill Mambe Nanje struggles
with the same problems as the workers do:

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:36.340
lack of money.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:43.400
“You need to pay them well so they don’t
move to bigger companies that will pay them higher.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:45.340
You need to motivate them.

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:49.400
What we do here is helping hundreds of thousands
of people.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:50.400
But that’s not enough.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:56.440
You need also to pay them a reasonable package
a month so that they stay.”

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:00.560
For Churchill Nanje, njorku.com is a mission.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:05.820
He wants to create opportunities for others and
hopes that other developers will follow his footsteps.

